# pinchtask

> [!WARNING]
> Almost all code is generated by GLM-5-Turbo. This program is provided as-is without any warranty.

A task management tool based on the Model Context Protocol (MCP), providing structured task management capabilities for AI Agents.

Supports three usage modes: **CLI local operations**, **TUI**, and **MCP server**, all sharing the same core business logic and data storage.

[中文文档](README.md)

## Features

- **Task Management** — Create, view, edit, and delete tasks with descriptions and shared context
- **Checklist System** — Each task contains ordered checklist items with full CRUD, mark complete/incomplete, and reordering
- **Notes** — Append free-form text notes to tasks
- **Resource References** — Link external documents, URLs, or file paths
- **Project Management** — Create, view, edit, and delete projects with task association (one-to-many)
- **Metadata** — Tags, priority (high/medium/low), and estimated completion time
- **Short ID Matching** — CLI supports entering the first 4+ characters of a UUID to locate tasks
- **Dual Mode** — Direct CLI operations / MCP stdio server for AI Agent invocation
- **JSON Output** — All query commands support the `--json` flag for machine-readable output
- **Interactive TUI** — Terminal interface based on ratatui with keyboard navigation, real-time search, and task management

## Installation

### Build from Source

```bash
# Requires Rust 1.70+ and Cargo
git clone https://github.com/Raven-1027/pinchtask.git
cd pinchtask
cargo build --release
# Binary is located at target/release/pinchtask
```

### Install via Cargo

```bash
cargo install --git https://github.com/Raven-1027/pinchtask
```

## Quick Start

### Create and Manage a Task

```bash
# Create a task
pinchtask task new "Implement user login" -c "Use JWT authentication"

# View task list
pinchtask task ls

# Add a checklist item
pinchtask item add <TASK_ID> "Design database schema" -d "users table and sessions table"

# Mark item as complete
pinchtask item check <TASK_ID> 0

# View progress summary
pinchtask item summary <TASK_ID>

# View task details
pinchtask task show <TASK_ID>
```

### Start MCP Server

```bash
# Run directly (auto-enters server mode when no subcommand is given)
pinchtask

# Or explicitly specify
pinchtask serve
```

## CLI Usage

```
pinchtask [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Global options:
  -D, --data-dir <DIR>      Data storage directory (default: ~/.pinchtask)
      --log-level <LEVEL>   Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
  -v, --verbose             Verbose output (equivalent to --log-level debug)
  -q, --quiet               Quiet mode (equivalent to --log-level error)
      --json                Output in JSON format

Commands:
  task        Task management (new, ls, show, edit, rm)
  item        Checklist item management (add, check, mv, summary, edit, rm)
  note        Note management (add, rm)
  link        Resource reference management (add, rm)
  project     Project management (new, ls, show, edit, rm, add-task, rm-task)
  serve       Start MCP server
  tui         Launch interactive TUI
  completion  Generate shell completion scripts
```

> For full command parameter details, see the [CLI Reference](docs/cli-reference.md).

## MCP Configuration

Configure in MCP-compatible AI clients (such as Claude Desktop, Cursor, etc.):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pinchtask": {
      "command": "pinchtask",
      "args": ["serve"],
      "env": {
        "PINCHTASK_DATA_DIR": "/path/to/data"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Or use `pinchtask` directly (defaults to server mode when no subcommand is given):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pinchtask": {
      "command": "pinchtask"
    }
  }
}
```

The server communicates with clients via **stdio** transport, supporting:

- Newline-delimited JSON format
- `Content-Length` header format

Protocol version: `2024-11-05`

## TUI Interactive Interface

Launch the terminal-based interactive interface via `pinchtask tui` and manage tasks using keyboard shortcuts.

### Launch

```bash
pinchtask tui
# Or specify a data directory
pinchtask tui -D /path/to/data
```

### Views

| View | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Task List | Display all tasks with search and sorting |
| Task Detail | View checklist items, notes, resources, and full info |
| Task Form | Create/edit tasks (Tab to switch fields, Enter to submit) |
| Help Panel | Display all keyboard shortcuts |

### Task List Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|----------|--------|
| `j` / `↓` | Move down |
| `k` / `↑` | Move up |
| `Enter` | View task details |
| `n` | New task |
| `d` | Delete task (requires confirmation) |
| `Tab` | Toggle sort mode |
| `/` | Enter search mode |
| `r` / `Ctrl+R` | Refresh list |
| `Home` / `End` | Jump to first/last item |
| `?` | Show help |
| `q` | Quit |

### Task Detail Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|----------|--------|
| `j` / `k` / `↑` / `↓` | Move focus |
| `Space` / `x` | Toggle item completion status |
| `a` | Add checklist item |
| `e` | Edit item name |
| `d` | Delete current item |
| `Ctrl+J` / `Ctrl+K` | Move item down/up |
| `N` (Shift+n) | Add note |
| `D` (Shift+d) | Delete note |
| `L` (Shift+l) | Add resource link |
| `E` (Shift+e) | Edit task |
| `Esc` | Return to list |

### Global Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|----------|--------|
| `Ctrl+C` | Force quit |
| `Esc` | Cancel / return to previous view |

## Data Storage

Task data is stored in a SQLite database file:

```
~/.pinchtask/
└── tasks.db
```

The database uses a hybrid normalization design: the `tasks` main table stores basic task information, `checklist_items`, `notes`, and `resources` are separate associated tables, and `metadata` is stored as a JSON column. The data directory can be customized via the `-D` parameter or the `PINCHTASK_DATA_DIR` environment variable. Tasks and projects have a one-to-many relationship — each task belongs to at most one project (via the `tasks.project_id` foreign key), and deleting a project automatically dissociates its tasks.

## Developer Guide

### Project Structure

```
src/
├── main.rs           # CLI entry point (error handling, exit codes)
├── lib.rs            # Library entry point
├── server.rs         # MCP server (request dispatch, tool registration)
├── store.rs          # SQLite persistence layer (sqlx async driver)
├── core/             # Pure business logic layer (shared by CLI, TUI, and MCP)
│   ├── mod.rs        #   Module entry point and public interface
│   ├── task.rs       #   Task-level operations
│   ├── item.rs       #   Checklist item operations
│   ├── note.rs       #   Note operations
│   ├── project.rs    #   Project-level operations (CRUD + task association)
│   └── resource.rs   #   Resource operations
├── models/           # Data models
│   ├── mod.rs        #   Module entry point
│   ├── task.rs       #   Task, ChecklistItem, Resource, TaskMetadata
│   └── project.rs    #   Project
├── protocol/         # MCP JSON-RPC protocol types
│   └── types.rs      #   Request/Response/ToolDefinition, etc.
├── transport/        # stdio transport layer
│   └── mod.rs        #   Newline-delimited JSON + Content-Length dual format support
├── tools/            # MCP tool adapter layer
│   ├── mod.rs        #   Module entry point
│   ├── params.rs     #   Tool parameter structs + json_schema_for() inline $ref
│   └── task.rs       #   Core layer unit tests
├── tui/              # Interactive terminal interface (optional feature)
│   ├── mod.rs        #   TUI entry point (terminal init, main loop)
│   ├── app.rs        #   Application state management, event handling
│   ├── event.rs      #   Event definitions and async event bus
│   └── ui/           #   Rendering module
│       ├── mod.rs           #     Main rendering entry (left-right split layout)
│       ├── task_detail.rs   #     Task detail rendering
│       ├── task_list.rs     #     Task list rendering
│       ├── project_form.rs  #     Project create/edit form
│       ├── project_list.rs  #     Project list rendering
│       └── theme.rs         #     Visual theme (colors, icons, progress bars)
└── cli/              # CLI command handling
    ├── mod.rs        #   Top-level argument parsing and nested subcommand dispatch
    ├── task.rs       #   task new / ls / show / edit / rm
    ├── item.rs       #   item add / check / mv / summary / edit / rm
    ├── note.rs       #   note add / rm
    ├── link.rs       #   link add / rm
    ├── project.rs    #   project new / ls / show / edit / rm / add-task / rm-task
    ├── output.rs     #   Unified output formatting
    ├── resolve.rs    #   Short ID prefix matching
    ├── logging.rs    #   Log initialization
    └── server.rs     #   serve subcommand
```

### Build & Test

```bash
cargo build
cargo test                # Run all unit tests
cargo test -- --nocapture # Show println! output
```

### Architecture Overview

```
User → CLI (clap) ──┐
                     ├──→ core (pure logic) ──→ store (SQLite + sqlx)
AI Agent → MCP ──────┤
User → TUI ──────────┘
```

All business logic is centralized in the `core/` layer. CLI, TUI, and MCP tools each act as adapter layers calling core functions, ensuring behavioral consistency.

### Exit Codes

| Code | Meaning                       |
| ---- | ----------------------------- |
| 0    | Success                       |
| 1    | General error                 |
| 2    | Task/project not found        |
| 3    | IO / database error / config error |

